Requirements: 7   with obligations: 7

[task-01] The `acceptance` command must find provider API keys in the `.env` file of the
    directory it is run from, wherever the tool itself is installed. Today it only finds
    them when it is run from inside its own source checkout: it has no `.env` loading of
    its own and depends on a library that searches for `.env` next to where that library
    is installed. Installed as a standalone tool and run in another project, it sees no
    keys at all.
    -> load-provider-keys-from-cwd-env  [functional/explicit]
       The acceptance command finds provider API keys in the `.env` file of the
       directory it is run from.

[task-02] When the command starts, it loads the `.env` file in the working directory, if
    there is one, before any model call. A variable already set in the environment keeps
    its value; `.env` only fills in what is missing. No `.env` file is not an error.
    -> load-env-before-model-call  [functional/explicit]
       Load the `.env` file in the working directory, if one exists, before any model
       call.
    -> preserve-existing-env-vars  [invariant/explicit]
       A variable already set in the environment keeps its value; `.env` only fills in
       what is missing.
    -> no-dotenv-file-is-not-an-error  [error_handling/explicit]
       The absence of a `.env` file is not treated as an error.

[task-03] A missing key must be reported clearly and early, never as the provider's
    "invalid API key" reply. In record mode, the command warns at startup about each key
    that a model it is configured to use would need and that is not set, naming the
    variable and the model. Before the first live call to a model, if that model's key
    is still missing, the run stops with an error that names the variable and the model,
    and the call is not sent. A run that needs no live call, because every request is
    already recorded or because it runs in replay mode, still succeeds without any keys.
    -> missing-key-reported-clearly-and-early  [functional/explicit]
       A missing key is reported clearly and early.
    -> clear-missing-key-reporting  [error_handling/explicit]
       A missing key is reported clearly and early, not as the provider's "invalid API
       key" reply.
    -> record-mode-warns-missing-model-keys-at-startup  [functional/explicit]
       In record mode, the command warns at startup about each key that a model it is
       configured to use would need and that is not set, naming the variable and the
       model.
    -> missing-key-stops-before-live-call  [error_handling/explicit]
       Before the first live call to a model, if that model's key is still missing, the
       run stops with an error that names the variable and the model.
    -> call-not-sent  [functional/explicit]
       The first live call to the model is prevented from being sent when the model's
       key is still missing.
    -> no-live-call-no-keys-required  [invariant/explicit]
       A run that needs no live call, because every request is already recorded or
       because it runs in replay mode, succeeds without any keys.

[constraint-01] No model request changes, so every recorded transcript keeps replaying.
    -> preserve-recorded-transcripts-replay  [compatibility/explicit]
       Preserve the ability for every recorded transcript to keep replaying without any
       model request changes.

[exclusion-01] Reading `.env` from any directory other than the working directory.
    -> no-other-env-directories  [compatibility/explicit]
       The change does not read `.env` from any directory other than the working
       directory.

[exclusion-02] Keys for the coding agent that builds mutation edits.
    -> do-not-read-coding-agent-keys  [functional/explicit]
       The change does not read keys for the coding agent that builds mutation edits.

[exclusion-03] A command-line option to name a different `.env` file.
    -> no-cli-option-for-env-file  [compatibility/explicit]
       The change does not add a command-line option to name a different `.env` file.

